[COMMAND]:      git.rm
[PACKAGE]:      GIT
[USE]:          dock -git rm

[OUT]:          Removes a remote from a local repository.

[ACTIONS]:      git remote rm origin

[NOTES]:        Upon executing this command, the reference remotes origin will no longer point to the 
                remote repository. It’s worth noting this does not delete your remote repository or affect 
                it in any way. All it means is that your local copy of a repository is no longer associated 
                with a particular remote. 
